---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Bump these by hand when the page content changes.
const updated = new Date('2026-10-08');
const sideLearningMonth = 'October 2026';

const fmt = (d: Date) =>
  d.toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Portfolio"
  description="Preah Smith's professional portfolio — Security+ certified cybersecurity graduate with Apple technical support experience and a self-hosted Proxmox homelab, working toward cloud security."
  active="portfolio"
>
  <!-- ---------- intro ---------- -->
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Portfolio</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      Cybersecurity graduate (B.B.A., UTSA) with CompTIA Security+ and A+, which makes me
      DoD 8140 IAT Level II eligible. I bring Apple technical support experience and run a
      Proxmox homelab with CI security scanning, monitoring, and SSO. I'm looking for IT support
      and security roles on the path to cloud security.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-cta">
      <a href="/files/preah_smith_resume.pdf" class="btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Resume (PDF)</a>
      <a href="mailto:contact@preahs.com" class="btn">contact@preahs.com</a>
      <a href="/docs" class="btn">Labs &amp; runbooks</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- featured projects ---------- -->
  <section class="block">
    <div class="block-head">
      <h2>Featured projects</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="case-list">
      <article class="case">
        <h3>Recovering an offline Proxmox host remotely</h3>
        <p class="case-summary">A dead NIC port took my hypervisor off the network. I diagnosed and fixed it out-of-band.</p>
        <dl>
          <dt>Problem</dt>
          <dd>The Proxmox host on my PowerEdge R730 dropped off the network, and every service on it went down with it.</dd>
          <dt>What I did</dt>
          <dd>I got in through iDRAC out-of-band access instead of the dead network path. I traced the outage to a failed NIC port, likely damaged by a flood-related power surge, then repointed the Proxmox bridge to a working port.</dd>
          <dt>Outcome</dt>
          <dd>I brought the host and its services back online without replacing hardware, and documented the recovery as a runbook.</dd>
        </dl>
        <ul class="tags"><li>Proxmox</li><li>iDRAC</li><li>Linux networking</li><li>PowerEdge R730</li></ul>
        <!-- TODO: write this runbook before deploying; slug must match the link below -->
        <a href="/docs/runbooks/proxmox-nic-failure" class="case-link">Read the runbook →</a>
      </article>

      <article class="case">
        <h3>Security scanning in CI</h3>
        <p class="case-summary">I built a Forgejo Actions pipeline that scans every push for leaked secrets and vulnerable dependencies.</p>
        <dl>
          <dt>Why</dt>
          <dd>I self-host my Git forge, so there's no GitHub-provided scanning. If a secret or a vulnerable dependency slipped in, nothing would catch it.</dd>
          <dt>What I built</dt>
          <dd>I wrote the workflows from scratch: Gitleaks for secret scanning and Trivy for vulnerability and misconfiguration scanning. Both run on a self-hosted runner in an LXC container.</dd>
          <dt>Result</dt>
          <dd>Builds are gated on scan results, so problems show up in CI before anything deploys.</dd>
        </dl>
        <ul class="tags"><li>Forgejo Actions</li><li>Gitleaks</li><li>Trivy</li><li>Docker</li></ul>
        <!-- TODO: write this runbook before deploying; slug must match the link below -->
        <a href="/docs/runbooks/ci-security-scanning" class="case-link">Read the runbook →</a>
      </article>

      <article class="case">
        <h3>Monitoring and alerting</h3>
        <p class="case-summary">Metrics, dashboards, and push alerts across the lab, plus a watchdog outside it.</p>
        <dl>
          <dt>Why</dt>
          <dd>I wanted to find out about failures before I noticed a service was down, including failures that take out the monitoring itself.</dd>
          <dt>What I built</dt>
          <dd>Prometheus collects metrics, Grafana shows them, and Alertmanager routes alerts to my self-hosted ntfy. An external VPS watchdog checks the site from outside, so I still get alerted if the whole homelab goes dark.</dd>
          <dt>Result</dt>
          <dd>Alerts reach my phone with no third-party services involved, and a full outage doesn't go unnoticed.</dd>
        </dl>
        <ul class="tags"><li>Prometheus</li><li>Grafana</li><li>Alertmanager</li><li>ntfy</li></ul>
        <!-- TODO: write this runbook before deploying; slug must match the link below -->
        <a href="/docs/runbooks/monitoring-and-alerting" class="case-link">Read the runbook →</a>
      </article>

      <article class="case">
        <h3>Nextcloud 403s after a bulk import</h3>
        <p class="case-summary">Writes failed everywhere while reads worked. The cause was Unix file ownership, not the app.</p>
        <dl>
          <dt>Problem</dt>
          <dd>After I copied files straight into the data directory, every upload, save, and new folder returned HTTP 403 from both web and iOS clients.</dd>
          <dt>What I did</dt>
          <dd>Because reads still worked, I ruled out the app's permission model and checked the filesystem. The import had run as root, so the web server user couldn't write to its own data directory.</dd>
          <dt>Outcome</dt>
          <dd>Correcting ownership and rescanning fixed writes. I wrote it up as a runbook with the diagnostic pattern to reuse.</dd>
        </dl>
        <ul class="tags"><li>Linux permissions</li><li>Nextcloud</li><li>occ</li></ul>
        <a href="/docs/runbooks/nextcloud-403-ownership" class="case-link">Read the runbook →</a>
      </article>
    </div>

    <h3 class="subhead">More projects</h3>
    <ul class="more-list">
      <li><strong>authentik SSO.</strong> Single sign-on in front of my self-hosted services.</li>
      <li><strong>LVM storage consolidation.</strong> Combined the homelab's storage into LVM volumes.</li>
      <li><strong>Matrix homeserver.</strong> Runs on a VPS at snowberry.social with a Discord bridge. <a href="/blog/homelab/starting-my-personal-matrix-homeserver" class="card-link">Write-up</a></li>
      <li><strong>The lab as a whole.</strong> <a href="/blog/homelab/overview-of-my-homelab" class="card-link">Overview of my homelab</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- currently building ---------- -->
  <section class="block">
    <div class="block-head">
      <h2>Currently building</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="now-grid">
      <div class="now-card">
        <span class="status">in progress</span>
        <h3>AWS Solutions Architect – Associate</h3>
        <p>My main focus right now: studying for the exam as the next step toward cloud security.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="now-card">
        <span class="status">in progress</span>
        <h3>Active Directory lab</h3>
        <p>
          A domain controller and a joined Windows 11 client at{' '}
          <a href="https://ad.snowberry.cloud" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ad.snowberry.cloud</a>.
          Domain fundamentals come first, then simulating and detecting common attacks (Kerberoasting,
          Pass-the-Hash, DCSync) mapped to MITRE ATT&amp;CK.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="side-learning">
      <h3 class="subhead">Side learning <span class="dates">— {sideLearningMonth}</span></h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Experimenting with k3s on a spare Dell machine to learn Kubernetes basics</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- skills ---------- -->
  <section class="block">
    <div class="block-head">
      <h2>Skills</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="skills-grid">
      <div class="skill-card">
        <div class="skill-head"><h3>Systems &amp; virtualization</h3><span class="depth">hands-on</span></div>
        <p>Proxmox, LXC, Docker &amp; Compose, Linux (Debian, Ubuntu), Windows, macOS, iOS</p>
      </div>
      <div class="skill-card">
        <div class="skill-head"><h3>Networking</h3><span class="depth">hands-on</span></div>
        <p>TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP, WireGuard, Tailscale, Cloudflare Tunnels</p>
      </div>
      <div class="skill-card">
        <div class="skill-head"><h3>Security</h3><span class="depth">hands-on</span></div>
        <p>Gitleaks, Trivy, authentik SSO, Nmap, Wireshark, MITRE ATT&amp;CK</p>
      </div>
      <div class="skill-card">
        <div class="skill-head"><h3>Monitoring &amp; CI/CD</h3><span class="depth">hands-on</span></div>
        <p>Prometheus, Grafana, Alertmanager, ntfy, Forgejo Actions, Git</p>
      </div>
      <div class="skill-card">
        <div class="skill-head"><h3>Scripting</h3><span class="depth">hands-on</span></div>
        <p>Bash, Python, YAML, HTML/CSS</p>
      </div>
      <div class="skill-card learning">
        <div class="skill-head"><h3>Learning</h3><span class="depth">in progress</span></div>
        <p>AWS, Active Directory, Kubernetes (k3s)</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- experience, certs, education ---------- -->
  <section class="block">
    <div class="block-head">
      <h2>Experience &amp; credentials</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-head">
          <h3>Technical Support Advisor <span class="org">— Apple (Remote)</span></h3>
          <span class="dates">Jan 2024 – Jul 2025</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Resolved 150+ cases a week across Mac, iPhone, iPad, and Apple Watch, covering hardware, OS, network connectivity, and account security issues</li>
          <li>Kept a 97% customer satisfaction rating in a high-volume environment, documenting every case in ticketing and CRM systems</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-head">
          <h3>Head Cashier <span class="org">— The Home Depot, Boerne, TX</span></h3>
          <span class="dates">Jan 2021 – Present</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Lead the cashier team and handle escalations for customer issues and POS failures, overseeing thousands of transactions a week</li>
          <li>Train new hires on POS systems, cash handling, and compliance procedures</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ed-grid">
      <div class="ed-card">
        <h3>B.B.A. in Cybersecurity</h3>
        <p class="org">University of Texas at San Antonio <span class="dates">— Aug 2026</span></p>
        <p>GPA 3.75 · Network Security, Information Assurance, Linux &amp; SQL</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ed-card">
        <h3>Certifications</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>CompTIA Security+ (SY0-701) <span class="dates">— Jun 2026</span></li>
          <li>CompTIA A+ (220-1201 &amp; 220-1202) <span class="dates">— Jan 2026</span></li>
          <li>DoD 8140 IAT Level II eligible</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="updated">Last updated <time datetime={updated.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}>{fmt(updated)}</time></p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .card-link,
  .case-link {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1.5px dashed var(--rule-strong);
    transition: border-color 0.15s;
  }

  .card-link:hover,
  .case-link:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--accent);
  }

  h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .dates {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .org {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .subhead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem;
  }

  /* ---------- featured case studies ---------- */
  .case-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 420px), 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .case {
    background: var(--paper-card);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.3rem 1.4rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.7rem;
  }

  .case h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .case-summary {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .case dl {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }

  .case dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
  }

  .case dd {
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .tags {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
  }

  .tags li {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.08em 0.5em;
  }

  .case-link {
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin-top: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  .more-list,
  .side-learning ul,
  .timeline-item ul,
  .ed-card ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .more-list li,
  .side-learning li,
  .timeline-item li,
  .ed-card li {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .more-list strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* ---------- currently building ---------- */
  .now-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 300px), 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .now-card {
    background: var(--paper-card);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.1rem 1.3rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }

  .now-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .now-card p {
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .status,
  .depth {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 1px solid currentColor;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.1em 0.6em;
  }

  .status {
    color: var(--folder);
  }

  /* ---------- skills ---------- */
  .skills-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 240px), 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .skill-card {
    background: var(--paper-card);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .skill-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .skill-card h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .skill-card p {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .depth {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .skill-card.learning .depth {
    color: var(--folder);
  }

  /* ---------- experience & credentials ---------- */
  .timeline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .timeline-item {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--rule);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .timeline-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.4rem 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .timeline-head h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .ed-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 280px), 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .ed-card {
    background: var(--paper-card);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.1rem 1.3rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .ed-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .ed-card > p {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  /* ---------- footer stamp ---------- */
  .updated {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }
</style>
